1
00:00:00,792 --> 00:00:05,797
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:13,179
-[gunshot]
-[Ivy] <i>You monster!</i>

3
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:15,432
<i>You buried my mother alive?!</i>

4
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,267
[Tonio] <i>But if your mother is still alive,</i>

5
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,061
<i>it's possible that the Ardientes have her.</i>

6
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:22,564
[Diego] <i>Why is she always with Mom?</i>
<i>What does she need from my family?</i>

7
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:23,982
<i>Why is she in Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

8
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,109
<i>Let's say that she is Lily.</i>

9
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:27,944
<i>Then why does she need to pretend?</i>

10
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,404
<i>That's what I need to find out.</i>

11
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,906
<i>Everything you've worked</i>
<i>so hard for is crumbling down.</i>

12
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>I don't know what to do. I need you.</i>

13
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:37,620
<i>Maybe this woman triggers</i>
<i>something from her past.</i>

14
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:40,165
[Raul] <i>Her memories can't return.</i>

15
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,416
<i>It might be better for her</i>

16
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:43,501
<i>to live as Jasmin</i>
<i>for the rest of her life.</i>

17
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,088
[Diego] <i>Who ordered you to do this?</i>

18
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:48,006
[man] <i>It's Natalie!</i>

19
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,258
<i>Thank you for coming to save me.</i>

20
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:52,677
<i>Good news. Your dad is awake.</i>

21
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:54,888
<i>What?! What will happen</i>
<i>when Papa comes back?</i>

22
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:57,140
<i>My life's going to be miserable again.</i>

23
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,184
<i>Papa has no reason to return here.</i>

24
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:01,144
<i>Or he shouldn't return at all.</i>

25
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:03,480
[Arnaldo] <i>Why didn't you tell me</i>
<i>Grandpa's recovered?</i>

26
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:04,898
<i>I'll tell Grandpa you were so busy</i>

27
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>taking over for him here.</i>
<i>I'm going to bring him home.</i>

28
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:11,529
-[whimpering] <i>Lily… Lily…</i>
-[Belen] <i>Jasmin?</i>

29
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:12,822
<i>Who is Lily?</i>

30
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,742
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, someone took my mom.</i>

31
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:18,703
<i>They replaced her with</i>
<i>another body to fake her death.</i>

32
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:19,829
[Jepoy] <i>What's your plan?</i>

33
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:23,625
[Ivy] <i>I'm going to dig up</i>
<i>all of Emilia's skeletons,</i>

34
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>and bring her fears to life.</i>

35
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:27,462
<i>You had a whole family murdered?</i>

36
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:28,713
<i>All of them.</i>

37
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:30,507
<i>Because when I tell my men</i>
<i>to do a good job,</i>

38
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,175
<i>it is indeed a good job.</i>

39
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:35,303
<i>Why are you so curious</i>
<i>about that family's story?</i>

40
00:01:35,386 --> 00:01:37,472
<i>Why all of a sudden, Ivy?</i>

41
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:43,728
Very good, Emilia. Very good.

42
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,563
I'm just testing

43
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:48,274
how you're going to answer
the press during your campaign.

44
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:52,153
And I think you're more than ready.

45
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:55,240
-Senator Emilia is ready.
-[chuckles]

46
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:58,535
So, tell me when you want to start,

47
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,537
so I can send my team here.

48
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:01,663
Thank you, Ivy.

49
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:04,124
You know, I really can't wait. Thank you.

50
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:05,875
You're most welcome.

51
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,335
[chuckles coyly]

52
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:09,921
Anyway, I have to go.

53
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:11,840
Okay. Oh, wait.

54
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,967
This weekend is Arnaldo's birthday.

55
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,135
Let's talk some more.

56
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:17,345
Mm-hm. Sure, Emilia.

57
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:18,513
Take care.

58
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:24,936
[tense music playing]

59
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:35,780
Grandpa, I'm sorry
I couldn't call earlier.

60
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:38,408
<i>I didn't know you were already</i>
<i>awake. Mom didn't tell me.</i>

61
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:40,994
[weakly] It's okay, grandson.

62
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:46,124
<i>We both know how incompetent</i>
<i>your mother is.</i>

63
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:49,168
<i>All she had to do</i>
<i>was pass down information…</i>

64
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:52,130
but she couldn't even do it properly.

65
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,133
Well, I think the reason is she
doesn't want you to come back.

66
00:02:56,301 --> 00:03:00,805
<i>She's not happy that I'm getting better?</i>

67
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:05,560
Well, she's been planning to
replace you in the senate bid.

68
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,770
Se-- [chuckles laboriously]

69
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:10,440
Senatorial bid.

70
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:14,193
That woman is delusional.

71
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:19,198
<i>Well, you know what they say.</i>

72
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:25,914
"When the cat is away…
the mice will play."

73
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:31,085
But don't worry, when the cat comes back…

74
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:38,509
he'll crush all of the mice's ambitions.

75
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,680
That's all they are…

76
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,935
ambitious mice.

77
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:50,063
[ominous music playing]

78
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:51,898
[exhales]

79
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,443
[ominous music playing]

80
00:03:58,488 --> 00:03:59,614
[exhales]

81
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,747
[inhales sharply]

82
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:15,755
[sinister music playing]

83
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:33,147
[sinister music playing]

84
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,657
[door lock rattling]

85
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,369
[Belen] Raul…

86
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:48,454
Do we really need to lock Jasmin up?

87
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,832
Can't she just stay here outside?

88
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:52,375
That's what's best for her.

89
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:58,631
[bangs on door, sobs]

90
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:01,551
It'd be better for her
to learn to talk again.

91
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,595
That's not true. I don't believe that.

92
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:06,139
You saw her, right?

93
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:08,141
It's just going to hurt her more.

94
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:11,102
And I don't care what the doctor said.

95
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:14,439
[sobbing]

96
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,151
[banging on door]

97
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:25,199
[sobs]

98
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:28,745
[pensive music playing]

99
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:32,874
Auntie, trust me, this is
what's best for Jasmin.

100
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:33,833
But, Raul…

101
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,918
Auntie, please just do as I say.

102
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:46,137
[sobbing]

103
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,600
[engine stops]

104
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:00,443
[grunting]

105
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:03,905
Diego?

106
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:10,578
[somber music playing]

107
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,876
<i>Ivy Aguas…</i>

108
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:21,172
<i>are you a mystery to me</i>
<i>because of my feelings for you,</i>

109
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:25,343
<i>or do I have feelings for you</i>
<i>because you're a mystery?</i>

110
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,683
[Ivy] Emilia won't elaborate on anything.

111
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,477
She's still a tough nut to crack.

112
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:38,356
But, dear, maybe she really
doesn't know anything.

113
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,191
It's possible.

114
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:43,277
But it's also possible she does,
and she's just good at hiding.

115
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:44,821
And Arnaldo?

116
00:06:47,448 --> 00:06:49,117
Arnaldo might be on to this, too.

117
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,327
I'm going to find out
at his birthday party.

118
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,662
How about you? What'd you learn?

119
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:55,123
Well…

120
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:58,126
I went to each of these
missing persons' houses…

121
00:06:58,584 --> 00:06:59,752
and I found out one thing.

122
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:02,338
Most of them were on Emilia's hit list…

123
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:05,091
-and Tonio was the hit man.
-Oh, god.

124
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,350
That's why we still need Tonio,

125
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:18,479
because he holds the answer
to my mother's whereabouts.

126
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:24,152
[tense music playing]

127
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,961
<i>Who are you, Ivy Aguas?</i>

128
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:46,841
[tense music playing]

129
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:03,149
[tense music playing]

130
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:21,083
[tense music playing]

131
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,965
<i>You never told me anything</i>
<i>about your family.</i>

132
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:30,927
<i>It's like you don't want</i>
<i>anyone entering your world.</i>

133
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,388
<i>Is that why you're avoiding me?</i>

134
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:38,768
[exhales]

135
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:43,439
-[door opens]
-[Ivy] Take care.

136
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:55,368
[tense music playing]

137
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:57,662
What are you doing here, Madrigal?

138
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:06,379
Mr. Mayor, you surprised me.

139
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:08,756
You even brought wine.

140
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,676
Is there something we need to celebrate?

141
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:14,262
I asked a question, I expect an answer.

142
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:16,472
What is Madrigal doing here?

143
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:19,308
Oh, no, Madrigal…

144
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:23,271
-Should we tell him now?
-What is going on?

145
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:26,190
[tense music playing]

146
00:09:34,156 --> 00:09:35,491
Mr. Mayor…

147
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:40,037
[sighs loudly]

148
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,291
I didn't want to tell him, but then…

149
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:46,669
I guess we don't have a choice, Madrigal.

150
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:52,341
We have to tell Mr. Mayor everything.

151
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:57,054
You see, Mr. Mayor…

152
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:04,520
I called your number one man over…

153
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:11,611
to ask him what kind of gift
you might like,

154
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,571
because your birthday's coming up soon.

155
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:17,450
A gift?

156
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:20,077
Yes, a gift.

157
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:21,537
But then…

158
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:26,042
all our efforts have gone
down the drain now, Mr. Mayor,

159
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:30,046
since you're already here
and found us out.

160
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:39,138
I just thought that you've given
me so many opportunities

161
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:41,724
here in Poblacion Ardiente.

162
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:43,351
So…

163
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:48,939
I thought of giving you a nice
gift to make it up to you.

164
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:53,653
But now, the cat's out of the bag.

165
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:57,406
Miss Aguas is right, Mayor.

166
00:10:57,698 --> 00:11:00,117
She called me over
to ask what your likes are.

167
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:04,121
So she could prepare her gift for you.

168
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:09,752
[tense music playing]

169
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,174
[clicks tongue] You really know
how to please, Miss Aguas.

170
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:16,258
[chuckles]

171
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,386
You didn't have to, but I appreciate it.

172
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:19,929
Well researched.

173
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,349
Of course.

174
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:28,396
But then, you already spoiled
our surprise, Mr. Mayor.

175
00:11:28,729 --> 00:11:29,855
I'm sorry.

176
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:32,108
[clicks tongue]
I just have to wait and see.

177
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:34,902
Okay.

178
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,320
[chuckles]

179
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:43,452
[tense music playing]

180
00:11:56,507 --> 00:12:00,010
[somber music playing]

181
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,141
[bangs on door]

182
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,435
[breathing heavily]

183
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:11,730
[sobbing]

184
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,816
[sobbing continues]

185
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,740
[breathing heavily]

186
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,535
Auntie, we need to go.

187
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:28,122
Pack up your things and Jasmin's.

188
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:30,166
We're going to leave this place.

189
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:31,250
But, Raul…

190
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,544
We're going to move somewhere else.

191
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,088
Just take your important stuff.

192
00:12:36,172 --> 00:12:37,089
Raul…

193
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:39,049
Auntie, I've already made up my mind.

194
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:44,763
[whimpers]

195
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:56,650
This is perfect.

196
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,987
You're in a good mood.

197
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,281
Of course, Auntie.

198
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:05,493
And that's because Ivy has
already vowed to support me

199
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:09,371
on my campaign to build up
the party's confidence in me.

200
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,332
So this is it. [chuckles]

201
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,250
I'm going to be a senator now.

202
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:15,586
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

203
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:22,051
But what if Julio comes back?

204
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,804
He can take everything away
from you, Emilia.

205
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:30,309
You should do everything that you have to.

206
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:34,813
Or else you will find yourself
back to your former life…

207
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,525
a slave to Julio.

208
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:39,193
Is that what you want?

209
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:42,655
[tense music playing]

210
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:51,747
[phone ringing]

211
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:56,877
Hello?

212
00:13:56,961 --> 00:14:02,132
What have you been screwing up
this time, Emilia?

213
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:03,759
[suspenseful sting]

214
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:05,386
Papa?

215
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:09,890
Yes, in the flesh.

216
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,645
Very much alive and kicking.

217
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:18,857
[suspenseful music playing]

218
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:24,697
He was one of Emilia's victims.

219
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,032
He worked in the municipal office.

220
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:29,952
He questioned her about the budget.

221
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:34,582
Yes, it was me. I killed him myself.

222
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,045
I killed this young man, too.

223
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:44,967
This one, too.

224
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:49,096
Did anyone order you to put
a ring on one of the corpses?

225
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,849
I only killed the victims.

226
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,101
But I'm not the one who buried them.

227
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:56,645
I don't know anything about a ring.

228
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:59,940
If you didn't bury them, then who did?

229
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:04,695
Mr. Noel.

230
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,864
He gathered the bodies,

231
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:10,034
and he's the one who dumped
and buried them, too.

232
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:17,875
And where can we find this Mr. Noel?

233
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:21,128
[tense music playing]

234
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:29,345
I know I've made a lot of mistakes, Papa.

235
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:33,349
But I did everything I could
to protect our name.

236
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:34,516
[Julio] <i>How?</i>

237
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:39,563
By proclaiming yourself as
the queen of Poblacion Ardiente?

238
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:44,360
<i>By throwing out and having</i>
<i>the farmers killed?</i>

239
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:49,823
Or having Senator Pablo murdered?

240
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:55,037
Is that how a decent leader acts?

241
00:15:56,121 --> 00:15:57,122
<i>No.</i>

242
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,793
Because that's what an executioner does.

243
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:04,672
<i>You disrespected our family's name.</i>

244
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:07,216
<i>This family has no room…</i>

245
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:12,554
for dumb and shallow people,
who make stupid decisions!

246
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:16,058
<i>Who do you think you are? Huh?</i>

247
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:21,438
Who told you to take over
everything I left behind?

248
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,399
Huh?! No one!

249
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:30,155
You have no right sitting
in my goddamn chair!

250
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,408
<i>Murdering my staff…</i>

251
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,910
and claiming my position!

252
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:39,248
You aren't even worthy enough
to lick my boot.

253
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:42,751
And when I return…

254
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:46,714
I will need a new set of canes.

255
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:48,924
<i>Because I assure you…</i>

256
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:51,135
that I will break every single one of them

257
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,721
while hitting that thick skull of yours

258
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,556
to see if your brain will still run…

259
00:16:56,098 --> 00:17:01,687
Or until you die and end up
on the roadside.

260
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,732
[suspenseful music playing]

261
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,867
[whimpers]

262
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:21,457
-[screams]
-[glass breaks]

263
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,876
[breathing heavily]

264
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:30,299
[suspenseful music playing]

265
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:36,930
[breathing heavily]

266
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:58,869
[ominous music playing]

267
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:10,130
Jepoy, you can go.

268
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:25,062
[instrumental theme music playing]

269
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:48,418
Dad…

270
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:51,755
It's been a while.

271
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:54,883
[inhales]

272
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:59,847
Dad, I think Mom is still alive.

273
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,644
I can feel it, Dad.

274
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:12,526
And I hope I'm right.

275
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:18,323
I really hope Mom is alive.

276
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:23,162
Because I miss her so much.

277
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,039
You too, Dad.

278
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,462
I miss our family.

279
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:34,756
[inhales sharply]

280
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,092
So, I really hope my hunch is right.

281
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:40,679
I hope that Mom is still alive.

282
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,268
I don't want to be alone anymore.

283
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,982
I want to be with Mom again.

284
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:55,360
I really miss you both.

285
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:59,239
I miss you both so much.

286
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,494
I love you, Dad.

287
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:10,876
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

288
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:15,005
I'll find Mom.

289
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,507
I promise.

290
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,012
[Jepoy] Walk faster.

291
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:24,306
Go on.

292
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:28,560
Ivy.

293
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:36,568
[tense music playing]

294
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,753
<i>I'm sorry, Camia.</i>

295
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:59,758
<i>I don't want to hurt you,</i>
<i>but I have to do this.</i>

296
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,345
<i>If I don't, I might lose you.</i>

297
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,931
<i>And I can't let that happen.</i>

298
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>Because someday, we'll build a family.</i>

299
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:15,023
<i>We'll be happy together.</i>

300
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,442
<i>I promise you that, Camia.</i>

301
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:26,868
[ominous music playing]

302
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:29,413
[Ivy] Noel.

303
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:31,248
You're Noel, right?

304
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,378
If you're the one who buries…

305
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:40,382
all of the Ardientes' victims…

306
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:45,762
then, are you…

307
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:49,683
are you the one who buried
my mother's body?

308
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:53,270
Who told you to do it?

309
00:21:55,772 --> 00:21:57,858
With all the bodies I buried…

310
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:01,320
how could I remember them?

311
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:08,035
Besides…

312
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:10,787
I've been living peacefully
as a gravedigger.

313
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:18,754
As they say, it's more peaceful
to deal with the dead…

314
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:22,507
than the living.

315
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:29,806
Now if that's all, I'll go now.

316
00:22:31,224 --> 00:22:34,102
It was 13 years ago
when they took my mother away.

317
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,729
[suspenseful sting]

318
00:22:36,396 --> 00:22:39,441
Someone claimed she was dead…

319
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:41,943
replaced her with another body…

320
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:44,404
and put her ring on it.

321
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:47,741
[tense music playing]

322
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:54,873
A ring?

323
00:22:57,834 --> 00:22:59,086
Did you say a ring?

324
00:23:06,426 --> 00:23:07,511
This one.

325
00:23:11,556 --> 00:23:14,476
[tense music playing]

326
00:23:19,856 --> 00:23:21,108
I remember it now.

327
00:23:29,366 --> 00:23:33,703
<i>A man asked me to bury</i>
<i>a sack of human bones.</i>

328
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:37,165
<i>Then he told me…</i>

329
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:44,673
<i>to put this exact ring</i>
<i>on one of the fingers.</i>

330
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:48,593
I remember it now.

331
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:52,180
Who told you to do it?

332
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,227
It was Raul.

333
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:00,730
Raul Torillo.

334
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:02,274
[suspenseful sting]

335
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:09,072
Raul Torillo?

336
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,199
The Raul Torillo?

337
00:24:11,908 --> 00:24:14,870
He was the man who gave me
the sack of bones.

338
00:24:16,454 --> 00:24:18,707
Why? Why would he ask you to do that?

339
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:19,833
I don't know.

340
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,334
[Jepoy] Listen to me.

341
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:23,336
Tell us the truth.

342
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:25,380
I really don't know. Believe me.

343
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,633
I was just following
the Ardientes' orders!

344
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,017
[Jepoy] Here.

345
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:42,272
I'm begging you…

346
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:46,026
Don't tell anyone about this conversation.

347
00:24:47,068 --> 00:24:49,863
I worked for them for nine years.

348
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:51,781
I just did what they told me.

349
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:56,328
I didn't know who they were
or why I have to bury them.

350
00:24:56,411 --> 00:24:59,289
[sobbing] But my conscience
is eating me up!

351
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:06,838
Maybe this is how
I can lighten the burden.

352
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:09,007
I pray…

353
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:12,469
that I was of help to you.

354
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:21,603
[tense music playing]

355
00:25:21,811 --> 00:25:22,812
Raul.

356
00:25:28,735 --> 00:25:29,861
It was Raul.

357
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:31,863
[breathing heavily]

358
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:44,834
Sit down.

359
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:53,301
[Raul clears throat]

360
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:58,765
Uh, love, I'm just packing up our things.

361
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:00,767
I'm packing because…

362
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,104
We're going to move somewhere else.

363
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:09,109
Somewhere new, bigger, and nicer.

364
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:12,404
[tense music playing]

365
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:17,575
Don't worry.

366
00:26:19,327 --> 00:26:21,079
I'll always be here for you.

367
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,081
I'll take care of you.

368
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:29,879
Then we're going away from here.

369
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:31,798
We're going to live happily.

370
00:26:35,510 --> 00:26:38,972
[tense music playing]

371
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:49,274
I just need to fix this.

372
00:26:52,986 --> 00:26:56,531
[tense music playing]

373
00:27:00,827 --> 00:27:02,537
[breathing heavily]

374
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:06,458
You're a monster, Raul! You--

375
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:09,085
You wretched bastard!

376
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:12,630
Dad, it was Raul!

377
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:15,425
Raul was the one who took Mom.

378
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:16,676
It was Raul.

379
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:19,262
Jepoy, everything started with Raul.

380
00:27:19,554 --> 00:27:20,555
The reason--

381
00:27:21,056 --> 00:27:22,932
He's the reason
why my family was targeted.

382
00:27:23,016 --> 00:27:25,518
Why my mom was mad at the Ardientes.

383
00:27:26,227 --> 00:27:28,063
This is Raul's fault.

384
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:30,815
And now, Raul has my mom.

385
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:35,528
Raul has my mom!

386
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:38,073
[breathing heavily]

387
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,033
Raul, you bastard…

388
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,620
You bastard.

389
00:27:46,206 --> 00:27:47,665
Get ready, Raul…

390
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:50,543
because I'm going to take my mom back.

391
00:27:52,754 --> 00:27:55,340
I'm going to take her back, Raul.

392
00:27:56,257 --> 00:27:57,509
[inhales sharply]

393
00:27:57,759 --> 00:27:59,260
It's Raul…

394
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,639
[screaming]

395
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:07,143
My mom is with Raul.

396
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:12,690
Dad, Raul has Mom…

397
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,693
Raul took Mom.

398
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:18,279
He's the one who took her.

399
00:28:18,696 --> 00:28:20,949
[whimpering]

400
00:28:22,158 --> 00:28:24,536
[Arnaldo] Okay, good.
Make sure that's complete.

401
00:28:27,455 --> 00:28:28,373
Mayor…

402
00:28:28,456 --> 00:28:30,250
The guests are arriving at the venue.

403
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:32,127
They're all excited for your birthday.

404
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:34,671
All right, good.
We're going to follow there.

405
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,214
Please entertain them in the meantime.

406
00:28:36,297 --> 00:28:37,715
-Yes, sir.
-Okay?

407
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:39,467
All right. Double time, everyone.

408
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:44,764
Wow, burgers.

409
00:28:45,265 --> 00:28:47,684
This is nice, Arnaldo.

410
00:28:48,643 --> 00:28:51,187
Burgers… for the Mayor's birthday.

411
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:53,398
What a brilliant idea,
don't you think, Ivy?

412
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:58,153
Happy birthday. But where's your father?

413
00:28:58,611 --> 00:29:00,280
-That's right.
-It's your birthday.

414
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:02,365
Is he coming, Mr. Mayor?

415
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:04,617
[Emilia] You know, Ivy has a point.

416
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:07,704
Your Daddy should be here
because, you know,

417
00:29:07,787 --> 00:29:11,416
it's the birthday of
Señor Julio's favorite grandson.

418
00:29:11,499 --> 00:29:14,210
You know, people might think
we have trouble in paradise

419
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:16,546
if he's not here, right, Ivy?

420
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:17,964
Where is he anyway?

421
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:22,010
[sighs]

422
00:29:22,343 --> 00:29:23,344
Arnaldo!

423
00:29:30,935 --> 00:29:32,687
Son, happy birthday.

424
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:36,107
Thanks.

425
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:39,778
I'm sorry. I'm a bit busy
with our business,

426
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:43,573
so I won't be able
to attend your birthday party.

427
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:46,201
[Arnaldo] You have to be there.
People will be looking for you.

428
00:29:48,119 --> 00:29:49,746
I can't promise that, son.

429
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:51,539
I really have to focus on the business.

430
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:54,501
That's why I came here
to tell you in advance.

431
00:29:55,543 --> 00:29:57,670
My goodness, Mr. Torillo.

432
00:29:57,754 --> 00:30:01,800
Are you saying you have more
important stuff to attend to

433
00:30:01,883 --> 00:30:03,009
than your son's birthday?

434
00:30:03,551 --> 00:30:05,762
[Emilia sighs] Ivy is right again.

435
00:30:06,179 --> 00:30:07,847
Is that errand of yours

436
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:11,184
more important than
your son's birthday, huh?

437
00:30:11,267 --> 00:30:12,685
Right. And lately, we've been noticing

438
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:14,187
you're always out of the house.

439
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:16,147
What have you been up to lately?

440
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:18,149
Like what I said,
our business has me swamped.

441
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:19,400
I have to focus on it, son.

442
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:22,278
But if we're going to have
problems because of that…

443
00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:25,615
if I really have to attend your
birthday, then I'll be there.

444
00:30:25,698 --> 00:30:27,784
Wow! How perfect.

445
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:31,663
Now we are one big happy family, right?

446
00:30:31,746 --> 00:30:32,789
Hmm…

447
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:39,879
-Happy birthday.
-Thank you.

448
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:42,090
-[Arnaldo] How are you?
-[man 1] Happy birthday, Mayor.

449
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:43,132
Thank you.

450
00:30:43,216 --> 00:30:45,260
-[woman] This is from the Mayor.
-How are you? How's the burger?

451
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,345
[Arnaldo] You can always get more, okay?

452
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:48,721
Just tell them I sent you.

453
00:30:49,347 --> 00:30:50,849
-[man 2] Thank you, Mayor.
-[Arnaldo] You're welcome.

454
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:52,767
-[man 3] Mayor, happy birthday.
-[woman 2] Happy birthday.

455
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:55,228
[Arnaldo] Thank you. Okay.
Go on, eat your fill.

456
00:30:55,311 --> 00:30:58,356
-Happy birthday, Mayor.
-Thank you, ma'am. Thank you.

457
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:01,734
Just get your burgers there.
They're for everyone.

458
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:03,486
-[woman 3] Thank you, Mayor.
-[Arnaldo] Okay, take a seat.

459
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:04,863
Happy birthday, Mayor.

460
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,447
-Thank you, thank you.
-[man 4] Happy birthday, Mayor.

461
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:08,032
-[Arnaldo] Thank you very much.
-Ivy, I'll just be there.

462
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:09,450
I have to talk to my constituents.

463
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:10,493
Okay, Emilia.

464
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:12,620
[Arnaldo] How are you? Are you okay now?

465
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:18,793
[Emilia] Give some more
to the people at the back.

466
00:31:19,127 --> 00:31:23,131
[tense music playing]

467
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:52,285
[tense music playing]

468
00:32:10,845 --> 00:32:11,846
[Diego] Ivy.

469
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:15,516
Diego.

470
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:16,935
Wait, I have to talk to you.

471
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,479
-Um, can we just talk later?
-Ivy.

472
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:22,398
This won't take long, Ivy.

473
00:32:24,651 --> 00:32:26,110
Uh, Diego…

474
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:27,570
Ivy, I didn't know you had a sister.

475
00:32:27,654 --> 00:32:29,739
[tense music playing]

476
00:32:29,822 --> 00:32:31,366
Why didn't you tell me?

477
00:32:32,325 --> 00:32:33,743
Why are you keeping secrets?

478
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:36,746
[scoffs]

479
00:32:38,498 --> 00:32:39,582
Uh…

480
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:41,834
[Ivy chuckles nervously]

481
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:44,170
Yes, Diego.

482
00:32:45,004 --> 00:32:46,255
I had a sister.

483
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,676
I didn't tell you about her

484
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:51,844
because it's still a very
sensitive topic for me.

485
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:55,306
I guess you won't understand

486
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:57,392
because you've never lost
a loved one before.

487
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:58,476
Ivy…

488
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:00,436
I know the feeling.

489
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:02,438
I've lost someone, too.

490
00:33:04,315 --> 00:33:06,567
Diego, Lily just disappeared.

491
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:09,278
She didn't die. They're different things.

492
00:33:11,739 --> 00:33:13,658
You never told me about that.

493
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:15,618
How did…

494
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:18,955
How did Lily and her family disappear?

495
00:33:22,166 --> 00:33:24,043
They went away without saying goodbye.

496
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:28,673
That's how they left?
Isn't that suspicious, Diego?

497
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:30,717
They didn't even say goodbye.

498
00:33:34,679 --> 00:33:38,433
All I remember is her parents
had a fight with my dad.

499
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:42,353
I guess they left because
they didn't want any trouble.

500
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:45,106
[sighs]

501
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:49,819
They didn't want any trouble? Why?

502
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,365
Did your dad hurt Lily and her family?

503
00:33:54,699 --> 00:33:56,951
Do you think your father
could do that, Diego?

504
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:58,244
Can he hurt other people?

505
00:33:59,954 --> 00:34:01,372
Is he that kind of person?

506
00:34:02,248 --> 00:34:05,793
[tense music playing]

507
00:34:06,335 --> 00:34:07,545
[sighs]

508
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:10,923
[inhales] Diego…

509
00:34:12,341 --> 00:34:15,261
I don't know why you're suddenly
interested in my sister.

510
00:34:17,013 --> 00:34:18,681
Are you doing a background check on me?

511
00:34:21,142 --> 00:34:23,102
Are you still doubting me?

512
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:29,734
[exasperated sigh]

513
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:33,279
It's sad, but I think the saying is true…

514
00:34:33,571 --> 00:34:35,907
that you can't please everyone.

515
00:34:37,116 --> 00:34:38,076
Ivy, I'm sorry.

516
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:40,078
It's not my problem anymore, Diego,

517
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:42,497
if you don't trust me.

518
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:46,626
Excuse me.

519
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:51,172
Ivy…

520
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,300
[tense music playing]

521
00:35:15,029 --> 00:35:16,364
[Arnaldo] Thank you very much

522
00:35:16,447 --> 00:35:19,158
for celebrating my birthday with me.

523
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:23,496
This day wouldn't be special
if it weren't for you.

524
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:26,499
Thank you very much.

525
00:35:26,582 --> 00:35:29,544
[crowd applauding]

526
00:35:29,627 --> 00:35:30,628
[woman] Happy birthday, Mayor.

527
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:33,965
[Arnaldo] And since everyone
is here already,

528
00:35:34,048 --> 00:35:37,677
and you're all part
of the Ardiente-Torillo family,

529
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:42,640
I'm sure everyone will be happy
to hear the news.

530
00:35:43,724 --> 00:35:47,270
My birthday wish was just
fulfilled earlier this day.

531
00:35:49,021 --> 00:35:54,193
I spoke to my grandfather's
doctor in America,

532
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:57,488
and he told me the good news,

533
00:35:57,572 --> 00:36:00,199
that Señor Julio is out of his coma.

534
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:04,579
And the doctor also told me

535
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:07,081
that my grandfather
is on the road to recovery.

536
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:09,125
Just a few more days…

537
00:36:09,709 --> 00:36:12,712
our beloved Congressman,

538
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:14,714
Señor Julio Ardiente, will return!

539
00:36:14,797 --> 00:36:18,551
[crowd applauding, cheering]

540
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:20,094
Viva Ardiente!

541
00:36:20,511 --> 00:36:23,431
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!
-One more! Viva Ardiente!

542
00:36:23,514 --> 00:36:24,849
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

543
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:30,688
[tense music playing]

544
00:36:37,236 --> 00:36:40,072
Once Julio sets foot
in Poblacion Ardiente,

545
00:36:40,656 --> 00:36:42,033
it'll be the end for you, Emilia.

546
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:43,826
You have to do something.

547
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:47,121
Auntie, I'm the one who's going
to be dead, not you.

548
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:50,166
I have a solution to all my problems here.

549
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:54,420
I'll treat him like one of my enemies.

550
00:36:59,759 --> 00:37:01,135
You're going to have Julio killed?

551
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:04,263
[tense music playing]

552
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:07,350
He's your father.

553
00:37:12,605 --> 00:37:15,024
Then I'll write him a nice eulogy.

554
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:18,861
I'll erect a big statue in his honor.

555
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:20,988
I'll even cry for him.

556
00:37:23,991 --> 00:37:28,871
But Poblacion Ardiente
is too small for the both of us.

557
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:33,000
[suspenseful music playing]

558
00:37:38,464 --> 00:37:39,465
Hello?

559
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:43,594
I have a new assignment for you.

560
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:50,810
Before this day ends, I want him dead.

561
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:57,858
[suspenseful music playing]

562
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:09,578
No, no, no, no!
I shouldn't have confronted her.

563
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:11,747
I shouldn't have asked about her sister.

564
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:15,543
It's only normal for you to ask.

565
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:17,295
You're friends.

566
00:38:17,837 --> 00:38:19,422
You're close, right?

567
00:38:19,505 --> 00:38:22,508
And it's like she's keeping
something from me, Nanny.

568
00:38:23,217 --> 00:38:25,094
What do you think it is?

569
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:28,139
I don't know, but I want to know her more.

570
00:38:28,222 --> 00:38:30,808
-[Loring] I understand.
-Because I love her, Nanny.

571
00:38:30,891 --> 00:38:31,892
What?!

572
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:34,729
Hey, hey, hey! That's something else!

573
00:38:34,812 --> 00:38:36,522
That's something else! [chuckles]

574
00:38:36,605 --> 00:38:38,649
-Hold on.
-Hey! Hey, wait.

575
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:39,734
Hey!

576
00:38:40,067 --> 00:38:41,152
Why, Diego?

577
00:38:41,235 --> 00:38:42,862
[giggles] Why?

578
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:45,990
Why don't you tell her?

579
00:38:46,073 --> 00:38:47,074
Just confess it.

580
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:50,161
Hey.

581
00:38:50,244 --> 00:38:51,370
[sighs]

582
00:38:51,454 --> 00:38:53,247
[both chuckle]

583
00:38:53,331 --> 00:38:54,332
I knew it.

584
00:38:54,623 --> 00:38:57,710
You know, you might be very handsome now.

585
00:38:58,085 --> 00:38:59,712
You might be taller and all.

586
00:38:59,795 --> 00:39:02,214
Your muscles might be bulging.

587
00:39:02,631 --> 00:39:06,385
But until now,
you are still the chubby Diego,

588
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:08,429
my shy little boy!

589
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:11,015
Diego, you have nothing to be ashamed of

590
00:39:11,098 --> 00:39:13,684
if your feelings are true!

591
00:39:13,768 --> 00:39:14,977
[Loring and Pandoy giggling]

592
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:16,187
[Pandoy] Come on.

593
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:18,314
[Loring] Tell her now how you feel.

594
00:39:18,773 --> 00:39:22,860
Confess your feelings so
she won't be mad at you anymore.

595
00:39:23,152 --> 00:39:24,153
Okay?

596
00:39:24,820 --> 00:39:27,031
So she'll understand. Who knows?

597
00:39:27,114 --> 00:39:28,574
She might tell you, "I love you, too."

598
00:39:28,657 --> 00:39:29,658
[giggles]

599
00:39:31,994 --> 00:39:33,079
[sighs]

600
00:39:34,580 --> 00:39:35,414
[exhales sharply]

601
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:49,678
[Julio] <i>Who told you</i>

602
00:39:49,762 --> 00:39:52,681
<i>to take over everything I left behind?</i>

603
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:57,645
<i>You have no right sitting</i>
<i>in my goddamn chair!</i>

604
00:39:57,728 --> 00:40:00,523
<i>You aren't even worthy enough</i>
<i>to lick my boot.</i>

605
00:40:00,606 --> 00:40:01,899
[Claire] <i>It'll be the end for you, Emilia.</i>

606
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:02,942
<i>You have to do something.</i>

607
00:40:03,025 --> 00:40:06,612
[Emilia] <i>Before this day ends,</i>
<i>I want him dead.</i>

608
00:40:06,695 --> 00:40:09,198
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[sniffles, sobs]

609
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:12,410
[laughing]

610
00:40:14,286 --> 00:40:16,330
[inhales, exhales sharply]

611
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:22,628
[suspenseful music playing]

612
00:40:22,711 --> 00:40:26,757
<i>Tonight, your problems</i>
<i>will finally disappear, Emilia.</i>

613
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:29,552
<i>I will miss you, Papa.</i>

614
00:40:31,470 --> 00:40:34,473
[laughing maniacally]

615
00:40:40,604 --> 00:40:44,608
[suspenseful music playing]

616
00:40:48,571 --> 00:40:50,573
[upbeat music playing]

617
00:40:51,490 --> 00:40:54,034
-[man 1] Cheers!
-[Arnaldo] Cheers! All right!

618
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:55,119
Nice.

619
00:40:57,455 --> 00:40:59,748
Great. I'm going to get some later.

620
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:02,710
How are my party-mates here?

621
00:41:02,793 --> 00:41:03,752
[man 2] Happy birthday, Mayor.

622
00:41:03,836 --> 00:41:06,464
[Arnaldo] We might not have our guns here,
but we can always go hunting.

623
00:41:07,047 --> 00:41:08,048
Arnaldo!

624
00:41:08,841 --> 00:41:09,925
Hey, Mom.

625
00:41:10,634 --> 00:41:13,262
-Happy birthday, son.
-Thank you. Thank you.

626
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:14,847
[Raul] Happy birthday, Arnaldo.

627
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:17,433
-Thank you.
-Enjoy your party, okay?

628
00:41:17,516 --> 00:41:18,601
I will.

629
00:41:18,684 --> 00:41:19,935
[Emilia] I'll just talk to some friends.

630
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:21,770
-[Arnaldo] Okay.
-[Raul] See you in a while.

631
00:41:21,854 --> 00:41:23,772
-Happy birthday.
-[Arnaldo] Thank you.

632
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:27,067
-Happy birthday, Mayor.
-Thank you.

633
00:41:29,945 --> 00:41:31,530
[Arnaldo] Take care of our guests.

634
00:41:31,697 --> 00:41:33,115
Just keep the alcohol flowing.

635
00:41:35,201 --> 00:41:38,287
Hi, Mr. Mayor. Happy, happy birthday.

636
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:39,580
Thank you.

637
00:41:40,956 --> 00:41:43,250
As promised… Surprise!

638
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:46,212
[Arnaldo chuckles]

639
00:41:48,881 --> 00:41:50,424
I hope you like it.

640
00:41:53,761 --> 00:41:56,931
-This is beautiful.
-[chuckles]

641
00:41:57,014 --> 00:41:58,140
Thank you very much.

642
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,934
I've been planning to buy
this gun ever since.

643
00:42:00,017 --> 00:42:01,727
And now I have it.

644
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:02,853
[chuckles]

645
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:04,980
Do you like it?

646
00:42:05,731 --> 00:42:06,941
It's perfect.

647
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:13,197
[upbeat music playing]

648
00:42:18,744 --> 00:42:21,830
Can I just say that you look
so beautiful tonight.

649
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:25,584
Thank you, Mr. Mayor.

650
00:42:26,043 --> 00:42:29,797
[upbeat music playing]

651
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:36,595
Take this inside.

652
00:42:38,889 --> 00:42:40,099
Happy birthday.

653
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:46,939
I don't remember inviting you,
but now you're here.

654
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:48,190
Thank you.

655
00:42:49,608 --> 00:42:50,651
Feel at home.

656
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:52,653
Enjoy the party.

657
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:54,780
We have a lot of women here.
I can introduce you.

658
00:42:57,950 --> 00:42:58,993
Excuse me.

659
00:42:59,076 --> 00:43:02,621
[upbeat music playing]

660
00:43:20,681 --> 00:43:21,890
[line ringing]

661
00:43:21,974 --> 00:43:22,933
[Raul] Hello?

662
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:27,104
All right. Just update me.
Don't let her out of your sight.

663
00:43:27,730 --> 00:43:30,649
Okay, I'll go there later.
Okay. Thank you.

664
00:43:38,240 --> 00:43:39,241
Hi.

665
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:41,160
Hi, Mr. Torillo.

666
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:43,078
-You look stressed.
-[Raul chuckles]

667
00:43:43,162 --> 00:43:46,582
Is something wrong?
Here, this one's for you.

668
00:43:47,166 --> 00:43:48,208
Thanks.

669
00:43:49,126 --> 00:43:51,253
Well, since you asked about my problems…

670
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:52,755
Yes, I have a lot.

671
00:43:53,672 --> 00:43:55,132
But it's none of your business.

672
00:44:00,763 --> 00:44:02,181
Mr. Torillo…

673
00:44:04,892 --> 00:44:06,268
It's your son's birthday.

674
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:07,436
Yeah, I know.

675
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:10,439
Let's have fun?

676
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:13,692
[chuckles]

677
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:16,695
You don't have to ask, Mr. Torillo…

678
00:44:18,530 --> 00:44:21,575
but I know a lot of ways
to relieve stress.

679
00:44:25,788 --> 00:44:27,623
You can wait for me here.

680
00:44:28,290 --> 00:44:29,541
-And then…
-[chuckles]

681
00:44:31,126 --> 00:44:32,336
I'll come back for you.

682
00:44:37,966 --> 00:44:38,967
Cheers?

683
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,305
Wait for me.

684
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:54,274
[tense music playing]

685
00:45:08,747 --> 00:45:11,208
Hey, wait a second.
I just need to use the toilet.

686
00:45:32,855 --> 00:45:35,190
[phone ringing]

687
00:45:37,526 --> 00:45:38,902
[line ringing]

688
00:45:39,278 --> 00:45:41,613
[phone ringing]

689
00:45:43,615 --> 00:45:45,993
[phone ringing]

690
00:45:48,579 --> 00:45:50,831
[phone continues ringing]

691
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:59,590
[phone continues ringing]

692
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:06,388
Hello?

693
00:46:08,265 --> 00:46:09,266
Hello?

694
00:46:11,894 --> 00:46:14,104
Hello? Are you with Camia Cruz?

695
00:46:14,313 --> 00:46:15,772
[suspenseful sting]

696
00:46:16,273 --> 00:46:17,274
<i>Hello?</i>

697
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:19,151
Hello?

698
00:46:21,862 --> 00:46:25,365
[suspenseful music playing]

699
00:46:28,035 --> 00:46:32,122
<i>Happy birthday, my favorite grandson!</i>

700
00:46:32,206 --> 00:46:34,082
<i>-How are you there in the States?</i>
-[Julio] <i>I'm good.</i>

701
00:46:34,166 --> 00:46:35,542
<i>And when I return,</i>

702
00:46:35,626 --> 00:46:41,089
<i>I will clean up the trash that</i>
<i>gathered there while I was away.</i>

703
00:46:41,173 --> 00:46:43,800
[Emilia] <i>He will regret coming back</i>

704
00:46:43,884 --> 00:46:45,802
<i>here to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

705
00:46:45,886 --> 00:46:49,765
<i>I will make his life a living hell.</i>

706
00:46:49,848 --> 00:46:51,391
<i>Mayor, some of our men saw Miss Aguas</i>

707
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:53,435
<i>following Mr. Raul outside</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

708
00:46:53,519 --> 00:46:54,478
[screaming]

709
00:46:54,561 --> 00:46:56,480
<i>-Raul, Jasmin got away!</i>
<i>-Where is Jasmin?!</i>

710
00:46:56,563 --> 00:46:57,564
[Belen] <i>Look for her!</i>

711
00:46:58,273 --> 00:46:59,149
<i>Mom?</i>

712
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:01,360
[tense music playing]
